From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:11:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: remove hosted account TUI commands

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Remove hosted account status, billing, and management commands from the TUI.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1012-personal-feature-remove-hosted-account-cli-commands.patch

Patch intent:
Remove TUI subscription status, account management, logout, and related slash
commands for hosted jcode accounts while retaining ordinary provider accounts
and direct API-key configuration.

Why it exists:
A local build must not present hosted billing, account, or subscription controls
in the interactive UI.

Upstream integration points:
The patch removes hosted account command parsing, dispatch, status rendering,
and asynchronous billing or revocation actions from TUI authentication code.

Update guidance:
Do not restore hosted subscription UI or slash commands. Preserve /login,
/logout, /account, and provider configuration for retained external providers.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode-tui
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-tui parse_account_doctor_subcommands --lib
